buildModel is operation
buildModel purpose "Group rows into entities by their `is` rows and enter each module-level entity's name in a map"
buildModel invariant groupsEntities "\"Each `<name> is <kind>` row starts an entity of that kind owning it and the rows after it up to the next `is` row; kinds are numbered module 1, capability 2, constant 3, operation 4, call 5, record 6, enum 7, typeInstance 8, region 9, task 10, table 11\""
buildModel invariant namesEntities "\"Each module's name maps to its position in the entity list, and each other entity's `<module>.<name>` to its position, except calls, tasks, and regions, whose names belong to the operation they are in\""
buildModel invariant rejectsOutsideModel "\"Another kind is unsupportedKind, a row whose subject is not the entity above it is strayRow, and a module-level name declared twice is duplicateName\""
buildModel typeParameter none
buildModel input source String borrowed
buildModel input words syntax.Words borrowed
buildModel input rows syntax.Rows borrowed
buildModel input entities Entities borrowedMutable
buildModel input names EntityNames borrowedMutable
buildModel output none
buildModel outputOwnedBy none
